+    "value": "Mastering (7-8): Explains that an NTC thermistor’s resistance falls as temperature rises, and that a potential divider produces a temperature-dependent analogue voltage; this must be converted by an ADC before the microcontroller can process it. Evaluates advantages (cheap, small, robust, wide temperature range, fast response). Evaluates disadvantages (non-linear response — resistance doesn't drop proportionally with temperature, requires calibration; analogue output needs ADC). Considers an alternative (digital temperature sensor IC such as DS18B20): direct digital output (no ADC needed), pre-calibrated, higher accuracy. Compares on cost, accuracy, integration complexity and food-safety regulatory context. Justified conclusion.\n\nSecure (5-6): Correct description of thermistor function, at least two advantages and one disadvantage, one alternative with brief comparison. Conclusion present.\n\nDeveloping (3-4): Basic description of thermistor. One advantage and one disadvantage. Limited alternative.\n\nEmerging (1-2): Simple identification of thermistor with minimal reasoning.\n\n[8 marks]",
